ach is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Reconcile the ADR filename with the parent epic: update the leaf's AC and Out-of-scope to reference `docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md` (or confirm the ADR was intentionally renumbered to 0115 across the epic and sibling tickets first).","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.575,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Leaf: 'docs/adr/0115-terraform-structural-grounding.md and docs/grounding.md distinguish V1 metadata probing from prohibited remote fetch'","Epic yaw-quota-wraith AC7: 'docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md records the trust boundary, OSS rationale, V1 prohibitions, and approved future ambient-credential remote-fetch direction'","Epic file_impact for docs/adr/0111-...: 'depraved-classless-rooster: record source trust boundary and approved-but-deferred ambient remote fetch'"],"finding":"The leaf names the ADR file as `docs/adr/0115-terraform-structural-grounding.md`, but the parent epic's AC7 and both the epic's and prerequisite's file_impact reference `docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md` as the single Terraform-grounding ADR the whole feature updates.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f402d4fda0cc6c2bc","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Leaf AC line 8 (`docs/adr/0115-...`) and 'Out of scope' ('The ADR records ambient-credential remote fetch as approved-but-deferred'); parent epic AC7 (`docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md`)","norm_id":"nabaac6c7b7fe28d5","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author edits/creates ADR 0115 while the feature's established ADR is 0111, splitting the trust-boundary record across two files or leaving the epic-designated ADR unupdated."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Change `docs/adr/0115-terraform-structural-grounding.md` to `docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md` in the leaf's Acceptance Criteria to match the epic's AC7 and file_impact.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In the ADR 0115 update, explicitly justify the V1 network+ambient-credential trust boundary against ADR 0115 §5 (why metadata-only ambient probing satisfies its intent rather than needing a separate gated step) and ADR 0063 (record the volume/shape/authority-style bounds — 1 MiB cap, 60 s deadline, no-redirect opener, positive-only, no-body/no-count receipt fields, auth_source-only logging — as the load-bearing contract, not merely a V1-vs-fetch distinction).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ADR 0115 §5: 'Ambient remote-fetch ... is deferred: it introduces a network trust boundary and a credential surface this slice's \"pure in-process, no external process\" decision (§1) is chosen to avoid. When taken up it must be an explicit, gated, non-ambient step with its own ADR.'","ADR 0063 Consequences: 'widening any of them (... adding a rebar-side fetcher that returns page bodies ...) reopens the exposure this ADR accepts ... and must be re-argued here.'","Plan: 'probe_source adds a bounded HTTPS helper ... returning status, final URL, and a size-capped body' — a rebar-side body-returning fetch, plus ambient TF_TOKEN/credentials.tfrc.json reads.","Web-confirmed prior art the plan DOES follow well: Terraform module/provider registry service-discovery protocol and the TF_TOKEN_<hostname> > CLI-config > credentials.tfrc.json precedence (developer.hashicorp.com).","deps.py confirms the internal oracle pattern (confirm-only, closed reasons, single _http_get seam) the plan repackages — that repackaging is justified; the network+credential trust-boundary decision is the part left unargued."],"finding":"The plan introduces a novel-for-this-codebase trust boundary — a credentialed, body-returning rebar-side HTTPS fetch with ambient CLI credentials — but does not explicitly justify that novelty against the two established internal precedents that bear on it (ADR 0115 §1's 'pure in-process, no network/credential surface' choice and ADR 0063's requirement that a rebar-side body-returning fetcher / outbound untrusted-response exposure be explicitly bounded and argued in an ADR).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5ffa7ae11211003f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → Registry metadata / Ambient credentials; AC line 'docs/adr/0115-... and docs/grounding.md distinguish V1 metadata probing from prohibited remote fetch and record ambient-credential fetch as approved-but-deferred'","norm_id":"nd542f9f4175968d7","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future reader/reviewer asks why ambient credentials + a body-returning fetch are acceptable in V1 when 0115 §5 said the successor step must be 'explicit, gated, non-ambient' with its own ADR.","Someone later 'tidies' the size/deadline/no-redirect/no-body-field bounds away because the ADR records them only as a V1-vs-fetch distinction, not as the load-bearing trust-boundary contract."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend the 0115 ADR-update AC so it records the metadata-probe network decision as a first-class trust-boundary entry: cite Terraform's registry service-discovery + credential-precedence protocols as the followed prior art, explain how positive-only + size/deadline/no-redirect/no-body-field bounds keep this narrower than the deferred remote-fetch of §5, and reference 0063's bounding pattern so the constraints cannot later be 'tidied' away without re-argument.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concrete platform-default CLI config path(s) the probe consults (per OS) so precedence item (2) is unambiguous and testable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.49,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"(2) `TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE` else platform-default CLI config\"","Terraform's default differs by OS (e.g. ~/.terraformrc / %APPDATA%\\terraform.rc), and the plan says only 'Follow Terraform's precedence' without pinning the resolved paths"],"finding":"The credential-precedence step names the 'platform-default CLI config' as fallback (2) but does not state the concrete default path(s) per OS the executor must resolve, leaving an OS-specific location to executor guesswork.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f53c367b5c8df0b72","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Ambient credentials section, precedence item (2) 'TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE else platform-default CLI config'","norm_id":"n3e9fcf689aaaa6ab","priority":0.11,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor implements a Linux-only default path and silently misses the Windows/macOS location, so a credentialed private host is treated as uncredentialed."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify whether probe_source's bounded HTTPS helper runs inline (like deps._http_get, monkeypatched in-process, urllib socket timeout) or inside harness.run_in_worker, and state which boundary enforces the 60s deadline vs a per-request urllib timeout — so the 'same monkeypatchable seam' and 'only DNS/socket faked' test oracle is realizable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.501,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["deps.py:_http_get is called INLINE (deps._probe_registry) with urllib timeout=10.0 and is monkeypatched directly in-process in tests/unit/grounding/test_deps.py (monkeypatch.setattr(deps, '_http_get', ...)); it does NOT run through run_in_worker","harness.run_in_worker uses multiprocessing 'spawn' and states 'func must be a module-level importable callable and its arguments ... must be pickleable' — a parent-process monkeypatch/env would not transparently apply in the child","harness._DEFAULT_TIMEOUT is 60s while the plan's cited deadline is 60s and deps.py's HTTP timeout is 10s; the plan does not reconcile which timeout governs the metadata fetch","Testing card: 'Production path: real ... response-parsing through the tool, only DNS/socket faked' — feasible inline, but ambiguous if the fetch is inside a spawned worker"],"finding":"The plan simultaneously says the HTTPS helper should 'reuse the grounding fail-open worker/harness' and be a 'bounded HTTPS helper (same monkeypatchable seam)', but the established network seam pattern (deps._http_get) runs INLINE with a urllib timeout and is monkeypatched in-process, whereas harness.run_in_worker spawns a subprocess (spawn context: pickleable module-level callable required; a parent-process monkeypatch and credential env do not cross that boundary identically). Which execution boundary probe_source's HTTPS call uses is unspecified and materially changes both the monkeypatch/test oracle and how the 60s deadline (harness _DEFAULT_TIMEOUT=60) relates to deps.py's inline 10s urllib timeout.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9543715cd9b7edd6","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → Registry metadata (\"reuse the grounding fail-open worker/harness and stdlib urllib\"; \"adds a bounded HTTPS helper (same monkeypatchable seam)\")","norm_id":"n61c7d10e39a9698a","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer wraps the HTTPS GET in run_in_worker; the test's in-process seam monkeypatch/credential env never reaches the child, so the DNS/socket-fake oracle and byte-scan cannot exercise the real path","Implementer follows deps.py inline pattern but then the '60-second deadline' and 'reuse the harness' language is unsatisfied, causing a mismatch with the stated bound"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Adopt the deps._http_get pattern: an inline private HTTPS helper (no-redirect opener, urllib socket timeout <= the 60s deadline, 1 MiB read cap) monkeypatched in-process, and reserve 'the harness' language for the existing parse worker only; drop or reword 'reuse the worker' for the network call.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name and verify (against Terraform's documented Registry protocol) the exact service-discovery, provider-versions, and module-versions endpoint paths the probe will call, and record them in the plan as MATCH/UNVERIFIED so the 'no download URL' test can assert the precise surface.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7625,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Use Registry service discovery and version/metadata endpoints only, never a download URL.'","AC: 'assert no download URL/archive endpoint is requested' — but no concrete endpoint path is named anywhere in the plan.","Precedent deps.py names its exact endpoint: `_DEPSDEV_BASE = \"https://api.deps.dev/v3/systems\"` and `url = f\"{_DEPSDEV_BASE}/{system}/packages/{quoted}\"`.","This is a NEW endpoint surface on a not-previously-used vendor (Terraform Registry); terraform_tools.py currently makes NO network calls."],"finding":"The plan asserts it will use Terraform 'Registry service discovery and version/metadata endpoints only, never a download URL' but never names the concrete endpoint paths (service-discovery well-known document, provider-versions endpoint, module-versions endpoint), leaving the specific external surface UNVERIFIED — unlike the deps.py precedent which names its exact endpoint (/v3/systems/{system}/packages/{name}).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f538e92c2869c6d7b","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope › Registry metadata; Acceptance Criteria (registry protocol tests / 'assert no download URL/archive endpoint is requested')","norm_id":"n898b6bd69fd47bfd","priority":0.1375,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementers pick the wrong discovery/version path from memory (e.g. a stale API version) and provider/module probing silently 404s → over-abstention, never a refute.","The 'no download URL requested' test can't be written precisely without the endpoint set being fixed in the spec."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add the concrete paths to the Registry-metadata scope: service discovery via `/.well-known/terraform.json` (to resolve `modules.v1`/`providers.v1` service URLs), then provider metadata via the discovered `providers.v1` + `<ns>/<type>/versions`, and module metadata via `modules.v1` + `<ns>/<name>/<system>/versions`; classify each as verified-against-docs (UNVERIFIED until confirmed) in the evidence.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the exact TF_TOKEN_<hostname> encoding transformation (dot and dash encoding, punycode for non-ASCII hosts) the probe implements, verified against Terraform's documented env-credential rule, and make the credential-precedence tests assert it.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7625,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '(1) `TF_TOKEN_<hostname>` env credential' and AC: 'Credential-precedence tests cover hostname encoding' — but the actual encoding transformation is never specified.","Terraform's rule is non-trivial (dots and dashes are encoded; non-ASCII hostnames use punycode), so 'hostname encoding' as a bare phrase is under-specified for an integration the plan asserts it follows exactly ('Follow Terraform's precedence and hostname normalization')."],"finding":"The plan relies on Terraform's TF_TOKEN_<hostname> environment credential but does not pin the hostname-to-env-var encoding rule (dots→underscores, dash handling, punycode for non-ASCII), leaving a precondition of the credential-precedence integration UNVERIFIED.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2fca0938f11e0304","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope › Ambient credentials; Acceptance Criteria (credential-precedence tests: 'cover hostname encoding')","norm_id":"n82ce866e72e7f26f","priority":0.1375,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer encodes only dots→underscores and misses dash-encoding/punycode, so a valid ambient TF_TOKEN_ var for a hyphenated or IDN registry host is never matched → credential silently absent → over-abstention on an authorized private registry."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_se